    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d380">

                <pb facs="0457" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1125</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d380-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 19, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> De Laboulaye<anchor n="2" xml:id="d380-f2"/> informs me that the French
                    Government has instructed the French Ambassador in Petrograd to inform Chicherin
                    (associated with Trotsky) indirectly that if the Bolsheviki resist the German
                    menace and defend Russia against the German aggression, France is ready to give
                    the Bolsheviki help in money and material. The French Government now inquire
                    whether the United States will give similar instructions to the American
                    Ambassador in Petrograd.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d380-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d380-f1-content">
                <p>Notes in the margin of MS.: “This is out of the question. R[obert] L[ansing].
                    Submitted to Pres[iden]t who says the same thing. R[obert] L[ansing]
                    2/19/18”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d380-f2" n="2" xml:id="d380-f2-content">
                <p>Second Secretary of the French Embassy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
